};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Brand Reviews",
    tags: [
      "truvani protein powder",
      "truvani plant protein",
      "truvani protein review",
      "truvani whey"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{
    text: "See Our Top Organic Picks",
    link: "/best-organic-protein-powder/",
  }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Brand Review
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Label-Checked
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Truvani Protein Powder: <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Organic and Simple, but Is It Enough?</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          A USDA Organic, monk fruit-sweetened pea protein with five ingredients, plus a newer three-ingredient organic whey. Here is what each delivers, which to buy, and what the heavy-metal reports mean.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#truvani-organic-plant-based-protein"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#whey"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Read the Label Breakdown
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">{author.name}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">{author.role}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#verdict" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. The Short Verdict</a>
          <a href="#plant-label" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. The Plant Protein Label</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. The Lineup</a>
          <a href="#whey" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. The Organic Whey</a>
          <a href="#which-one" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Which Truvani to Buy</a>
          <a href="#cost" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Cost per 25 g of Protein</a>
          <a href="#metals" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Heavy Metals and Prop 65</a>
          <a href="#who-skip" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Who Should Skip Truvani</a>
          <a href="#compare" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. How Truvani Compares</a>
          <a href="#use" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Using Truvani Well</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">12. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Truvani makes one of the shortest, cleanest organic protein labels you can buy, but its flagship plant protein gives only about 20 g per scoop at a premium price, and independent testing has found heavy metals in it. Buy it for the ingredient list and the organic seal, and go in knowing those two trade-offs.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="verdict" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Short Verdict
          </h2>

          <p>
            Truvani is a clean-label wellness brand co-founded by Vani Hari, the food activist known online as the Food Babe. Its pitch is simple: products made with a handful of organic ingredients and nothing its founders consider unnecessary, which in practice means no stevia, no gums, no artificial sweeteners and no added sugar. Protein is its best-known product, alongside collagen and other supplements.
          </p>

          <p>
            The flagship is Truvani Organic Plant Based Protein. The vanilla flavor lists about 20 g of protein per scoop in roughly 130 calories, from organic pea protein with organic pumpkin seed and chia seed protein, sweetened with organic monk fruit, per the HEB and Amazon listings at the time of writing. It is certified USDA Organic and free of dairy, soy and gluten. The brand has more recently added an organic whey protein with about 20 g of protein from three ingredients.
          </p>

          <p>
            Those are genuinely short labels, and for buyers who read every ingredient they are a big draw. The trade-offs are dose, price and testing. Twenty grams is below the 25 g many people aim for per shake, the cost per 25 g of protein is high, and a lead-safety advocate's lab tests have found lead, cadmium and arsenic in Truvani plant protein samples. Those findings are not unusual for plant proteins, but they are worth knowing.
          </p>

          <p>
            Our verdict: Truvani is a good choice for organic, minimal-ingredient buyers who want a plant protein without stevia, and the organic whey is a smart addition for anyone who eats dairy. If you want the most protein per dollar, or a sport certification, the options in our <a href="/best-organic-protein-powder/">best organic protein powder</a> guide offer more.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">THE VERDICT</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">A beautifully short organic label at a modest dose and a premium price</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">About 20 g of organic pea-based protein with monk fruit and five ingredients, around 130 calories. Worth buying for clean-label and stevia-free shoppers. Skip it if cost per gram or heavy-metal exposure is your priority.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="plant-label" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What Is in the Plant Protein
          </h2>

          <p>
            The vanilla plant protein's ingredient list is five items long: organic pea protein, organic vanilla powder, organic pumpkin seed protein, organic monk fruit extract and organic chia seed protein, per retailer listings at the time of writing. The chocolate version adds organic alkalized cocoa, and other flavors swap in ingredients such as organic banana powder and Ceylon cinnamon. It is hard to find a flavored protein with a shorter list.
          </p>

          <p>
            Per the HEB label for the vanilla tub, one scoop gives about 20 g of protein, 130 calories, 3 g of fat, 5 g of carbohydrate including 2 g of fiber, and 2 g of sugar, with about 20 servings per container. Whole Foods marketing copy gives a range of 120 to 140 calories across flavors. Sodium on the vanilla label is about 280 mg per scoop, relatively high for a plant protein, so check it if you are tracking salt.
          </p>

          <p>
            Pea is the main protein, and pea is one of the better plant sources: it is rich in lysine and reasonably high in leucine, though lower in methionine than animal proteins. Pumpkin seed and chia add a little protein of their own and help round out the amino acid profile. A 20 g scoop of a pea-led blend delivers less leucine than 20 g of whey, which is one reason plant-protein buyers often benefit from a slightly larger dose.
          </p>

          <p>
            Monk fruit is the only sweetener. That is the brand's clear differentiator: many clean-label plant proteins use stevia, which some people find bitter, and Truvani avoids it entirely. Buyer feedback on taste is mostly positive for a plant protein, though some buyers note the earthy, slightly gritty texture that pea proteins commonly have when mixed with water alone. Our <a href="/best-pea-protein-powder/">best pea protein powder</a> guide explains how pea compares with other plant sources.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Label figure</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Vanilla plant (per scoop)</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">What it means</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Protein</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 20 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Below the 25 g many people target</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Calories</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 130</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Typical for a plant blend</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Protein source</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Organic pea, pumpkin seed, chia</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Pea-led plant blend</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Sweetener</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Organic monk fruit</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">No stevia, no added sugar</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. The Truvani Protein Lineup, Ranked
          </h2>

          <p>
            These are the Truvani protein powders we could confirm on Amazon at the time of writing, flagship first, followed by two organic alternatives from other brands for buyers who want more protein per scoop or a lower cost. Figures are per the label at the time of writing and vary by flavor.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                    <span class="bg-[#FF4500] text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-black">
