          </p>

          <p>
            Against Garden of Life Sport Organic Plant-Based Protein, Truvani loses on dose and verification. Garden of Life delivers about 30 g of organic plant protein per serving and carries NSF Certified for Sport status, per the brand and NSF at the time of writing, though its label is longer. For athletes, Garden of Life is the stronger organic pick; see our <a href="/garden-of-life-protein-powder-review/">Garden of Life protein powder review</a>.
          </p>

          <p>
            Against Just Ingredients, another clean-label brand, the difference is the protein base. Just Ingredients is whey-led with collagen and coconut milk, creamy but higher in saturated fat. Truvani's plant protein is lighter and dairy-free, and its whey is simpler still. Our <a href="/just-ingredients-protein-powder-review/">Just Ingredients protein review</a> goes through that brand's label.
